    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18057280/005056a3-d347-1fe1-ac8f-3786dfb182bd": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Technical Analysis & CET)",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Technical Analysis & CET) – School of Business | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Technical Analysis & CET) – School of Business Fixed Terms Closing on 12 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only will he/she have both the knowledge and working experience, he/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing them, and moulding their characters. There will be opportunities to develop the curriculum, introduce new modules/courses as well as be involved in consultancy and other applied research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job too.  Successful candidates will be expected to have a growth mind-set, and be adaptable to the ever-changing industry landscape, both in the domain industry as well as the education sector. He/she is also expected to demonstrate resourcefulness and innovative with forward-looking initiatives as well as good communication skills. This is for a full-time role. The appointee must be competent to teach in areas of Technical Analysis, as well as the following Banking and Finance related areas: •\tCorporate Finance •\tCredit Risk Analysis and Management •\tInternational Trade Finance •\tWealth Management What you will be working on Responsibilities: Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) students. Keep abreast of current developments and trends in the areas mentioned above to develop and maintain relevant and up-to-date teaching curriculum. This includes review of existing curriculum with a view to making recommendations on areas of improvements that would enhance students’ performance, learning & employability. Enhance students’ learning through other activities such as training students for competitions, supervising projects, and internships, and leading them on overseas learning programme/community service. Identify new partnership opportunities, building industry partnerships, and cultivating industry relationships. Participate in consultancy projects with industry partners to support the transformation of the industry. Collaborate with other staff as well as industry to offer meaningful applied industry projects and consultancy projects. Support IBF / SkillsFuture initiatives in the implementation of Enhanced Internship Programmes and CET programmes. Handle administrative work relating to teaching. What we are looking for Requirements: At least 3 years of relevant working experience across financial institutions such as banks, brokerages, and/or insurance companies. Part-time experience in education would be an added advantage. Strong passion in mentoring students and show genuine concern for their development. A strong team player with good communication skills Proven ability to engage with the industry on Banking/Finance/Analytics/Fintech consultancy projects. Relevant qualifications in Banking/Finance/Analytics/IT or equivalent such as  MFAS/CACS/CFA/CAIA would be an added advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 12 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
